        "answer": {
          "short": "Range: $y\\geq1$.",
          "worked": "The curve has vertical asymptote $x=0$, with $y\\to\\infty$ as $x\\to0^+$. Also $y\\to\\infty$ as $x\\to\\infty$. There are no intercepts. The curve decreases to its minimum $(1,1)$, then increases, changing from concave up to concave down at $\\left(2,\\frac12+\\ln2\\right)$. Hence the range is $[1,\\infty)$.",
